<title>GERMANY: Germany's Walter wins Australian contract.</title>
<headline>Germany's Walter wins Australian contract.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Walter Bau-AG said on Thursday its Australian subsidiary Concrete Constructions Group Ltd had received contracts worth 103 million marks.</p>
<p>The largest single contract, worth 70 million marks, is for the construction of infrastructure for the &quot;Homebush Bay&quot; Olympic site in Sydney which will host the Olympic Gamnes in the year 2000.</p>
<p>Walter Bau owns 75 percent of Concrete Constructions.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
